For the first time, we are hosted in the PoliMi space dedicated to events.

It's a new venue in a very nice part of the city, let's gather and have some fun with Zig!

We have limited seats because it's not meant for workshops, there's limited room for tables.
Please manage the RSVP carefully, if you can't join, even at last minute, let us know through the event management page on meetup.com.

# Goals for the day

The primary goal is learning and sharing knowledge!
You should be able to finish the day taking away a novel concept about Zig or systems programming.

This can be done in various ways, here is a non-exhaustive list:

* Free-form building software collaboratively
* Discuss the Io concurrency and asynchrony model of 0.16.0
* Work in pair or mob on an existing Zig project
* Explore the documentation and read the standard library source code

All the attendees are encouraged to learn Zig if they are new to the language, or mentor newcomers if they are already proficient with the language.

# RSVP

Sign up to the event via [meetup.com](https://www.meetup.com/italia-zig-user-group/events/316611598/).
